WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.140
I know it sounds crazy, but Monkey D. Garp might&nbsp;
not be Luffy’s only legendary grandpa. because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:11.760
what if I told you that his grandfather&nbsp;
on the other side of the family tree was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:17.640
none other than Rocks D. Xebec? And I promise&nbsp;
that if you make it to the end of this video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:25.560
you will have you’re mind completley blown&nbsp;
away. Big thanks to reddit user Mr. Bushido&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:30.360
for laying the groundwork for this theory on&nbsp;
our subreddit about the secret Goa Kingdom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:36.000
connection between Garp, Rocks, and&nbsp;
Roger and their brotherly friendship.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:43.620
But before we can get to the crazy parts, we have&nbsp;
to do some ground work first. Because really,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:50.520
we don’t know all that much about this most&nbsp;
infamous of all pirates trying to conquer the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:59.280
one piece world who was all but erased from&nbsp;
history. However his silhouette alone should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:04.080
tell us something. Lots of theorists have&nbsp;
drawn the obvious Blackbeard comparisons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.640
Teach’s giant raft literally being&nbsp;
named the Saber of Xebec. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:16.320
Rocks’s silhouette looks a whole lot like&nbsp;
another character we know: Monkey D. Dragon.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.540
A lot of fans had long assumed that Monkey D.&nbsp;
Dragon was Garp’s son, given that he carries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:31.560
the Monkey family name. However, this might not&nbsp;
be the case. Garp never once refers to Dragon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:39.900
as his “son” - he only ever refers to him&nbsp;
as “Luffy’s father.” Dragon could very well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:47.940
be Garp’s son-in-law and Luffy’s mother could be&nbsp;
Garp’s daughter. Luffy even strongly resembles his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:55.140
grandfather, but those genes seem to have skipped&nbsp;
Dragon’s generation entirely if Dragon was in fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.140 --> 00:02:02.640
Garp’s biological son. Could it be that after&nbsp;
Rocks was erased from history, Dragon instead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:08.220
took his wife’s name - the daughter of Garp and&nbsp;
Luffy’s mother? It wouldn’t be the first time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:14.880
a character has taken their mother’s name. After&nbsp;
all, Luffy’s own brother, Ace, was named Portgas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:23.640
as a way of separating him from Roger’s lineage&nbsp;
for his own protection. Could Dragon and then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:29.760
Luffy after him have done the same in order to&nbsp;
separate themselves from the Rocks family name?

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:35.640
And while Dragon clearly has different goals&nbsp;
than Garp, his vision does seem to align&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:42.120
with part of Rocks. Dragon doesn’t appear to&nbsp;
want to claim the Empty Throne for himself to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:48.660
become the king of the world, but like Xebec,&nbsp;
he does specifically want to combat the World&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:56.820
Government and the Celestial Dragons. Could he&nbsp;
have inherited this will from Rocks? After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:03.060
the D clan are the natural enemies of the&nbsp;
Celestial Dragons, just as we see in Luffy.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:09.420
This isn’t the only thing that Luffy would seem to&nbsp;
have inherited from the Rocks side of the family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:15.600
though. We know that Rocks gathered into&nbsp;
his crew the most fearsome pirates on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:22.380
Grand Line. Edward Newgate. Charlotte Linlin.&nbsp;
Shiki the Golden Lion. Even a young Kaidou. All&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:27.540
of these pirates, many of whom would become&nbsp;
yonkou, the strongest forces on the planet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:34.200
all served on Rocks’ ship. Someone&nbsp;
who could rally all of these forces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:43.560
under one flag would have to be supremely&nbsp;
charismatic - they would have to have a gift&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:49.140
of making friends and allies out of anyone&nbsp;
they’d meet. Sound like anyone you know?

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:56.580
According to Mihawk, Luffy’s propensity for&nbsp;
making allies is his greatest strength. And this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:01.980
strength may have come from his grandfather,&nbsp;
Rocks D. Xebec. In the same way that Rocks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:07.320
gathered the strongest pirates of the era&nbsp;
to his side, so Luffy does by amassing his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:12.120
grand fleet and teaming up with several&nbsp;
members of the Worst Generation. Law and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:17.760
Kid seem very much to be set up as similarly&nbsp;
significant members of Luffy’s own pirate era.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:24.600
The similarities between Rocks D. Xebec, Monkey&nbsp;
D. Dragon, and Luffy are multifaceted. Not only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:31.740
do they share physical resemblances, but they&nbsp;
share defining characteristics as well. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:38.220
that’s not where this theory ends. *Laughs* Not&nbsp;
even close. The ending is going to blow you away.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:43.980
So let’s talk about Luffy’s family tree. Because&nbsp;
the family history shared between the Monkey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:51.960
and Rocks clans might go way, way deeper so get&nbsp;
ready for some Soap Opera levels of speculation.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:05:00.060
It all starts with young Garp. Eiichiro Oda has a&nbsp;
really tight grasp on his story’s timeline. Even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:05.580
when there are potential loopholes, he’s pretty&nbsp;
good about closing them. After he decided to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:10.320
Ace the son of Gol D. Roger (a move that was&nbsp;
most likely not intended from the beginning),&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:16.620
he knew it wouldn’t work because Roger&nbsp;
had died before Ace’s birth. Ergo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:23.700
Portgas D. Rouge was pregnant for two years to&nbsp;
avoid the One Piece equivalent of King Herod.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:28.020
This is a man who, when he introduced time&nbsp;
travel into the series, made sure that it only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:33.720
worked one way so he wouldn’t mess up his precious&nbsp;
timeline. He even uses masterful hints like having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:39.900
the samurai and Momo alluding to knowing Roger,&nbsp;
allowing eagle eyed readers to guess the huge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:46.140
time travel plot twist. So given that Oda has been&nbsp;
very meticulous, let’s look at Garp in the past.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:55.620
When Oda drew Garp as a child, he looked&nbsp;
a whole lot like young Luffy. He’s a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.620 --> 00:06:02.160
rambunctious adventurer riding a tiger. He’s a&nbsp;
wild boy befriending forest animals just like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:09.720
his grandson. This doesn’t look like a future&nbsp;
hero of the marines - this looks like a future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:18.780
pirate. So how did he go from the spitting image&nbsp;
of Luffy to a Marine? And more importantly let’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:24.660
poke at his timeline a little bit. He joined&nbsp;
the marines at the age of 22. We know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:30.960
Koby joined the Marines at the young age of 16.&nbsp;
Zephyr from Film Z joined the Marines at age 14.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:36.240
And while it’s not unheard of for marines to&nbsp;
join later on in life, Sakazuki and Boraslino,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:41.940
for instance, were also in their 20s when&nbsp;
they joined, it is clear that joining the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:50.580
marines wasn’t exactly the starting point for&nbsp;
Garp. What might Garp have been doing up until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:54.600
age 22? This is going to be super imortant for&nbsp;
the crazy conclusion of this theroy at the end.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:05.940
Luffy clearly takes after his grandpa, so&nbsp;
it’s doubtful that Garp was just patiently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:12.480
waiting around the Goa Kingdom into his&nbsp;
20s. If he was anything like Luffy as a kid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:18.900
which the illustration would suggest,&nbsp;
he probably couldn’t wait to get away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:24.360
from his home island and see the world.&nbsp;
But before we speculate on what exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:30.060
Garp was doing for all those years, let’s&nbsp;
talk about that home island a little more.

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:36.120
The Goa Kingdom is a place of extreme&nbsp;
inequality. The nobles live in complete&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:41.760
extravagance while the poorest members of the&nbsp;
country live among the literal trash of the Gray&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:46.620
Terminal. We don’t know exactly what inspired&nbsp;
Garp to become a marine in the first place,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:51.720
but his foundation here could have instilled&nbsp;
a desire to create a better, more just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:56.460
world - while at the same time reinforcing&nbsp;
his conflicted distrust of the World Nobles.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:03.960
Dragon, who also hails from Goa Kingdom, sees it&nbsp;
as a microcosm for the entire One Piece world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:09.840
But unlike Garp who wants to improve the system&nbsp;
from within, his “son” or probable son-in-law,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:14.880
Dragon wants to take down the whole of the corrupt&nbsp;
World Government and rebuild a better world.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:27.180
When naming the nationalities of the&nbsp;
Straw Hats if they were real-life people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:34.380
Oda has said that Luffy would be Brazilian.&nbsp;
The Goa Kingdom actually takes its name from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:39.000
a region of India that was colonized&nbsp;
by Portugal, the same European country&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:45.420
that colonized Brazil. But what if I told you&nbsp;
that Oda giving Luffy’s nationality might have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:50.880
actually been one of the biggest pieces&nbsp;
of foreshadowing in the entire series.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:59.580
It’s common knowledge that many One Piece pirates&nbsp;
are named after real life pirates. X-Drake is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:05.760
Sir Francis Drake. Jewelry Bonney is Anne&nbsp;
Bonney. Blackbeard is…Blackbeard. But one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:12.900
parallel I haven’t heard as much is Rocks. Rocks&nbsp;
seems like an extremely strange name, but there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:23.700
actually was a famous pirate named this: Roche&nbsp;
Brasiliano. In English, his name is literally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:30.360
Rock the Brazilian. The Brazilian…as in…from&nbsp;
Brazil. And Rocks even shares a few important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:38.520
qualities with his real-life counterpart. He&nbsp;
sailed with some very other famous and notorious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:44.460
pirates - such as Henry Morgan -Captain Morgan’s&nbsp;
namesake for the rum fans in the audience. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:49.620
first mate Jelles de Lecat or “Captain Yellows”&nbsp;
became a mighty pirate captain in his own right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:55.380
just like the yonkou who were spawned from the&nbsp;
former Rocks crew. Roche Brasiliano even bought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.380 --> 00:10:04.020
his ship from Francois L’ollonais - Roronoa&nbsp;
Zoro’s namesake. That part’s just a fun fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:09.600
though…we highly doubt that Rocks bought&nbsp;
his ship from a yet-to-be-born Zoro.

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:20.160
Roche was famously barbaric and violent, drunken&nbsp;
and debaucherous. But the crucial similarity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:28.560
is in Rock the Brazilian’s fate. No one knows.&nbsp;
There is no record of him after 1671 - whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:37.440
he died at sea or retreated into a quiet life of&nbsp;
anonymity, his fate is unexplained. Just as Rocks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:45.780
and God Valley have been wiped from history books,&nbsp;
Roche Brasiliano’s end is shrouded in mystery.

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:51.540
Could Rocks be from the Goa Kingdom, One&nbsp;
Piece’s Brazil equivalent? And if so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:56.520
then who’s to say that Rocks D. Xebec and&nbsp;
Monkey D. Garp met each other on the high&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.520 --> 00:11:03.360
seas? As a pirate and a marine? It’s hard to&nbsp;
envision Garp as anything but the hardheaded,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:09.720
fist of love wielding marine we know and love,&nbsp;
but could Rocks and him have been friends? If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:14.100
they are from the same kingdom, it would be&nbsp;
believable that two super-powerful people with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:19.980
outsized personalities would at least know&nbsp;
each other, if not get along. And if Garp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:25.440
shared Luffy’s adventurous disposition, could&nbsp;
they even have voyaged together out to sea?

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:30.960
What if during Garp’s missing years before&nbsp;
joining the Marines at the age of 22 he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:37.920
actually a pirate? Not a violent buccaneer, of&nbsp;
course, but a peaceful and adventurous pirate like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:42.540
his grandson. Or if we use the terminology from&nbsp;
Romance Dawn, the one shot that Oda released as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:50.640
precursor to One Piece, a Peacemain pirate,&nbsp;
as opposed to the violent Morganeers. And,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:56.280
of course, we already know of Garp’s connection&nbsp;
to Gol D. Roger. While being fierce rivals - the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.280 --> 00:12:03.240
hero of the marines and the king of the pirates -&nbsp;
they were also close friends. Roger trusted Ace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:12.120
his own son, into Garp’s care. Not&nbsp;
Rayleigh or Shanks or any other pirate:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:18.600
Garp. Roger is also from the East&nbsp;
Blue, hailing from Loguetown. Could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:24.600
the two upstarts from the Goa Kingdom,&nbsp;
Rocks and Garp, have met Roger as well?

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:33.240
I know it sounds absolutely insane, but try to&nbsp;
entertain the idea that before the formation of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:37.980
the Rocks crew, before Roger found the One&nbsp;
Piece, and before Garp joined the Marines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:49.320
the three all sailed together on one ship. The&nbsp;
three could have adventured and sought treasure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:55.260
and thrills sailing from island to island.&nbsp;
But eventually, something changed. A rift&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.260 --> 00:13:02.760
formed between the three friends. Likely, the&nbsp;
conflict was brought on by Rocks. This is pure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:07.620
speculation since we won’t know until we finally&nbsp;
learn the truth behind Rocks and what happened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:14.280
between the three at God Valley. Xebec likely&nbsp;
was no longer satisfied with simple fun-loving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:20.880
adventuring. He wanted Wealth. Fame. Power.&nbsp;
And perhaps he would stop at nothing to achieve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:26.700
them. He would treat others cruelly. He would&nbsp;
enact violence on his rivals and perhaps even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:31.200
innocent people. And you should really subscribe&nbsp;
if you don’t want Xebec coming for you next.

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:36.240
And this great division that formed&nbsp;
between these three friends sent Roger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:43.620
and Garp in separate directions, too. Roger&nbsp;
insisted that piracy could still be fine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:49.380
but done in the right way. He could still&nbsp;
adventure and be free without bringing harm to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:54.240
others. And gather together with Silvers Rayleigh,&nbsp;
Scopper Gaban, and the rest of the Roger pirates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.240 --> 00:14:00.540
he circumnavigated the entire globe,&nbsp;
eventually finding Laugh Tale. Garp,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:06.960
however, wanted to protect others from the harm of&nbsp;
violent pirates like Rocks and chose to join the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:12.420
Marines. Despite his inner conflict with working&nbsp;
under the Celestial Dragons, he sought to work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.420 --> 00:14:17.220
within the system to change it for the better -&nbsp;
given that Koby and Helmeppo have joined SWORD,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:23.400
and were also trained under him, Garp’s a&nbsp;
good candidate for this organization’s leader.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:33.540
The three went their separate ways, but would&nbsp;
meet again. When Rocks set his eyes on becoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:38.340
king of the world, the World Government had&nbsp;
to stand in opposition to him. Ever since we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:43.860
learned about God Valley, it’s been perplexing&nbsp;
to think that Roger and Garp would ever team up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:50.640
yet alone do so to protect the Celestial Dragons.&nbsp;
Garp is clearly no fan of the Celestial Dragons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:59.340
but it might just be that they weren’t fighting&nbsp;
Rocks to save the World Nobles at all. They were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:04.140
fighting to prevent a world where&nbsp;
Rocks held the power because such&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:07.740
a world would be even worse than one&nbsp;
controlled by the World Government.

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:18.060
This theory makes God Valley personal.&nbsp;
Garp and Roger weren’t just fighting a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:21.660
terrible and powerful enemy - they&nbsp;
were fighting against their closest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:28.080
friend and brother. It’s no stretch of the&nbsp;
imagination to think that these three would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:28.080 --> 00:15:37.260
have exchanged sake cups just like Sabo, Ace,&nbsp;
and Luffy eventually would. This would raise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:41.760
the stakes of an eventual Rocks and&nbsp;
God Valley flashback so much higher.

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:47.940
These three legends of the One Piece world -&nbsp;
an evil pirate, a marine hero, and the king of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:53.940
the pirates might even parallel similar trios&nbsp;
today. The new Rocks would be Blackbeard, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.940 --> 00:16:00.180
future Pirate King would of course be Luffy, and&nbsp;
the Marine Hero role could be fulfilled by Smoker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:05.340
or more likely based on recent story events,&nbsp;
Koby. After all, Luffy and Koby have been friends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:11.760
and allies all throughout the series - even before&nbsp;
Luffy gathered a single member of his pirate crew.

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:16.320
If this theory is true and Luffy is&nbsp;
the grandson of both Rocks and Garp,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:24.420
this would mean he inherited the D initial from&nbsp;
both sides of his family tree. The only other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:30.120
character who is confirmed to have a D from&nbsp;
both his paternal and maternal lines is Ace.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:35.940
Clearly they were both the optimal candidates to&nbsp;
become the next pirate king and the next Joyboy.

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:42.540
But this of course leaves us with another and&nbsp;
maybe even bigger mystery. If Rocks and Garp&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:49.800
are Luffy’s Grandfathers and Dragon his dad, who&nbsp;
in the world is Luffy’s mother? And who are his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:55.440
grandmothers? As his family tree seems to become&nbsp;
more and more significant - and with Oda-sensei&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:55.440 --> 00:17:02.160
having confirmed twice now that he *has* drawn&nbsp;
Luffy’s mother already in the series, shouldn’t it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:09.480
be possible to figure out who it is? And yeah, it&nbsp;
is. So, click this video if you wanna watch that.

